  "mcpOnlyConcepts": {
    "tasks": {
      "treatment": "adapter-blocks-internally",
      "note": "MCP Tasks (pollable tools) have no n8n async-task equivalent. The adapter calls the tool and polls to completion internally before returning to the node — the same behavior the SDK's own taskSupport:'optional' path already gives a non-task-aware client. Pollable tools still resolve to a normal resource+operation (Story 8.1), never excluded for this reason alone."
    },
    "authFailSoft": {
      "treatment": "no-n8n-equivalent",
      "note": "MCP's missing-credential fail-soft (boot + tools/list, clear error only on call) has no n8n equivalent — n8n's own credential system requires credentials configured before a node can execute at all. The adapter's native credential validation supersedes fail-soft entirely; no adapter-side accommodation is needed."
    },
    "toolAnnotations": {
      "treatment": "pass-through",
      "note": "Spec-compliant tool annotations (destructiveHint/readOnlyHint/idempotentHint, Epic 4) are informational, not exclusionary — the adapter may use them for its own UI treatment (e.g. a confirmation prompt on a destructive operation), but this project makes no assumption about how; they are not a reason to n8nExclude a tool."
    }
  }
